WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.599
The authors test PatchRot on four standard image
classification datasets: CIFAR-10,

00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:09.910
CIFAR-100, FashionMNIST at thirty-two by thirty-two
resolution,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:13.058
and Tiny-ImageNet at sixty-four by sixty-four.

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:18.464
They also study SVHN and MNIST to probe
rotation-invariant objects like digits.

00:00:18.544 --> 00:00:23.185
The backbone is a compact vision transformer with
six encoder blocks.

00:00:23.265 --> 00:00:28.591
Patch sizes are four pixels for the small datasets
and eight for Tiny-ImageNet,

00:00:28.671 --> 00:00:32.218
with a buffer gap set to a quarter of the patch size.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.134
Beyond plain classification,

00:00:34.214 --> 00:00:38.444
they evaluate transfer learning between CIFAR-10
and CIFAR-100,

00:00:38.524 --> 00:00:43.440
and a semi-supervised setting on CIFAR-10 where
only a handful of labels,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:47.340
from two hundred fifty up to ten thousand, are available.
